        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Can you buy the Reebok FR20z in the US?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not easily, as of 14 October 2026. Reebok’s US fitness store showed no treadmills and its FR20z page no longer loaded, and the FR20z listings we checked on Amazon’s US site were marked currently unavailable. Other US retailers have listed it. If you find one, confirm it is a US-voltage unit with a warranty honoured in the US.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Reebok FR20z fold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. The official Reebok Fitness listings state that it is not foldable, and most independent reviews list the fixed deck as a drawback for small spaces. It needs a permanent footprint of about 177 by 69 cm, roughly 70 by 27 inches, plus clearance behind the belt. Transport wheels let you roll it short distances.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit on the Reebok FR20z?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The maximum user weight is 120 kg, about 264 lb, on the official listings, independent reviews and the Amazon US listing title. As a rule of thumb, choose a machine rated comfortably above your body weight, so users near that figure should look at a model with a higher rating and a wider belt.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How fast does the Reebok FR20z go?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Up to 18 km/h, which is 11.2 mph or a pace of about 5 minutes 21 seconds per mile. That covers walking, easy running and most tempo running for recreational runners. Faster runners doing short intervals may find it limiting, which is the main speed criticism in independent reviews.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Reebok FR20z work with Zwift?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. It connects over Bluetooth and is listed as compatible with Zwift and Kinomap. Neither is required to use the treadmill, and both are separate paid services. Some listings include a free Kinomap trial, but the length varies between 30 and 60 days depending on the listing, so check the current offer.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does the Reebok FR20z have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It depends on where you buy it. An Australian retailer lists two years on the frame and twelve months on parts, UK reviews cite ten years on the motor and two years on parts and labour, and a US retailer listing gave ten years on the frame. Ask the seller for the terms that apply in your country, in writing.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
